{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The policy sets a deliberately asymmetric matcher: exact identifiers override everything; strong aliases behave as names; weak aliases require an identical full DOB; DOB conflicts veto otherwise valid names; and ambiguous valid candidates resolve by identifier, then DOB support, then UID. I’m now mapping the development variation classes and the register’s language/name patterns so the normalization is precise without turning into unsafe fuzzy matching."}}
