{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"agent_message","text":"The unlabeled-batch audit is behaving well: every unmatched full-DOB record that still shares a register DOB is now a genuine different-name look-alike, while unregistered-identifier match rates align with the labeled sample. I’m broadening the catalog romanization layer systematically (not with edit distance): German/Polish/French Cyrillic spellings and assimilated Arabic/Persian forms found across the batch, then re-running the full negative sample after each expansion."}}
